# Murmur – Child Safety Standards

**Effective Date:** November 26, 2026

## 1. Our Commitment to Child Safety

Murmur is committed to providing a safe social networking environment. We have zero tolerance for child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE), child sexual abuse material (CSAM), grooming, or any form of exploitation of minors.

## 2. Prohibited Content and Behavior

Murmur strictly prohibits:
- Child sexual abuse and exploitation.
- Sharing, distributing, or promoting child sexual abuse material.
- Sexual exploitation or grooming of minors.
- Attempts to solicit or exploit minors.
- Content that facilitates the abuse, trafficking, or exploitation of children.

## 3. Reporting Child Safety Concerns

Users must be able to report accounts and content involving suspected child exploitation through Murmur's in-app reporting mechanism.

Reports will be reviewed by the designated moderation team. Appropriate action may include removing content, restricting accounts, and escalating serious cases to the appropriate authorities.

## 4. Moderation and Enforcement

Murmur will investigate reported child safety violations and take appropriate action against accounts that violate these standards.

Violations may result in content removal, account suspension, or permanent account termination.

## 5. Legal Compliance and Reporting

Murmur is committed to complying with applicable child safety laws and regulations. Where legally required, confirmed cases of child sexual abuse material will be reported to the appropriate regional or national authorities.

Murmur will cooperate with relevant authorities in accordance with applicable laws.

